title: binary ninja architecture and platform
url:   https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html
tags:  binaryninja binja bn arch architecture platform cpu os callingconvention abi python api

; arch = Architecture, plat = Platform. Names in UPPERCASE are placeholders.

## architecture
Architecture["x86_64"]    # get an architecture by name (x86, armv7, thumb2, aarch64, mips32...)  @cpu @isa  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture>
list(Architecture)        # list all architectures  @cpu  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture>
bv.arch                   # get the architecture of a view  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.BinaryView.arch>
arch.name                 # get the architecture name  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture>
arch.address_size         # get the pointer size in bytes  @bits  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture>
arch.endianness           # get the byte order  @endian  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture>
arch.max_instr_length     # get the longest possible instruction in bytes  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture>
arch.regs                 # get a dict of register name to RegisterInfo (size, full-width reg)  @registers  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture>
arch.full_width_regs      # list the full-size registers only (rax, not eax)  @registers  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture.full_width_regs>
arch.stack_pointer        # get the stack pointer register name  @sp @rsp  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture>
arch.link_reg             # get the link register name (lr on ARM)  @return-address  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture>
arch.flags                # list the flag names  @eflags @cpsr  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture>
arch.intrinsics           # get a dict of intrinsic name to info (special instructions)  @builtin  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture>
arch.calling_conventions  # get a dict of calling conventions for the arch  @abi  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture.calling_conventions>
arch.standalone_platform  # get the OS-less platform for the arch  @baremetal @firmware  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture.standalone_platform>

## disassemble and assemble
arch.get_instruction_text(DATA, ADDR)     # disassemble bytes to (tokens, length)  @disasm @decode  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture.get_instruction_text>
"".join(str(t) for t in arch.get_instruction_text(DATA, ADDR)[0])  # disassemble bytes to one text line  @disasm @print  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture.get_instruction_text>
arch.get_instruction_info(DATA, ADDR)     # get length and branch targets of an instruction  @branch @decode  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture.get_instruction_info>
arch.get_instruction_low_level_il(DATA, ADDR, il)  # lift one instruction into an LLIL function  @lift  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture.get_instruction_low_level_il>
arch.get_low_level_il_from_bytes(DATA, ADDR)  # lift bytes to an LLIL instruction without a view  @lift  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture.get_low_level_il_from_bytes>
arch.assemble("mov eax, 1", ADDR)         # assemble text to bytes  @asm @patch @keystone  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture.assemble>
arch.can_assemble                         # check if the arch has an assembler  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture.can_assemble>
arch.convert_to_nop(DATA, ADDR)           # get NOP bytes that replace an instruction  @patch  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture.convert_to_nop>
arch.get_reg_index("rax")                 # turn a register name into its index  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture.get_reg_index>
arch.get_reg_name(INDEX)                  # turn a register index into its name  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture.get_reg_name>

## platform
Platform["linux-x86_64"]                  # get a platform by name (windows-x86, mac-aarch64, linux-armv7...)  @os  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.platform-module.html#binaryninja.platform.Platform>
list(Platform)                            # list all platforms  @os  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.platform-module.html#binaryninja.platform.Platform>
Platform.get_list(os="linux")             # list platforms for one OS or arch  @os  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.platform-module.html#binaryninja.platform.Platform.get_list>
bv.platform                               # get the platform of a view  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.BinaryView.platform>
plat.name, plat.arch                      # get the platform name and its architecture  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.platform-module.html#binaryninja.platform.Platform.name>
plat.default_calling_convention           # get the default calling convention  @abi @cdecl  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.platform-module.html#binaryninja.platform.Platform.default_calling_convention>
plat.system_call_convention               # get the syscall calling convention  @syscall  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.platform-module.html#binaryninja.platform.Platform.system_call_convention>
plat.system_calls                         # get a dict of syscall number to (name, type)  @syscall  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.platform-module.html#binaryninja.platform.Platform.system_calls>
plat.get_system_call_name(NUM)            # get a syscall name by number  @syscall  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.platform-module.html#binaryninja.platform.Platform.get_system_call_name>
plat.types                                # get a dict of the platform's built-in types (libc, Win32)  @headers  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.platform-module.html#binaryninja.platform.Platform.types>
plat.get_type_by_name(NAME)               # get a platform type by name  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.platform-module.html#binaryninja.platform.Platform.get_type_by_name>
plat.get_function_by_name(NAME)           # get a known API prototype from the platform  @signature @import  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.platform-module.html#binaryninja.platform.Platform.get_function_by_name>
plat.get_related_platform(Architecture["thumb2"])  # get the sister platform for another arch (ARM/Thumb)  @interworking  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.platform-module.html#binaryninja.platform.Platform.get_related_platform>
plat.type_libraries                       # list type libraries for the platform  @bntl  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.platform-module.html#binaryninja.platform.Platform.type_libraries>

## calling conventions
plat.calling_conventions   # list the platform's calling conventions  @abi  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.platform-module.html#binaryninja.platform.Platform.calling_conventions>
cc.name                    # get the convention name (cdecl, sysv, win64...)  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.callingconvention-module.html#binaryninja.callingconvention.CallingConvention>
cc.int_arg_regs            # list registers used for integer arguments  @args @abi  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.callingconvention-module.html#binaryninja.callingconvention.CallingConvention>
cc.int_return_reg          # get the integer return register  @ret @abi  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.callingconvention-module.html#binaryninja.callingconvention.CallingConvention>
cc.callee_saved_regs       # list callee-saved registers  @nonvolatile  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.callingconvention-module.html#binaryninja.callingconvention.CallingConvention>
cc.caller_saved_regs       # list caller-saved registers  @volatile @clobber  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.callingconvention-module.html#binaryninja.callingconvention.CallingConvention>
f.calling_convention = cc  # set a function's calling convention  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.function-module.html#binaryninja.function.Function.calling_convention>

## custom architecture (plugin)
class MyArch(Architecture):               # write a new architecture: set name, regs, override 3 methods  @plugin @processor  <https://docs.binary.ninja/dev/archplatform-architecture.html>
    def get_instruction_info(self, data, addr) -> InstructionInfo  # length and branches
    def get_instruction_text(self, data, addr) -> (tokens, length)  # disassembly
    def get_instruction_low_level_il(self, data, addr, il) -> length  # lifting
MyArch.register()                         # make a custom architecture available  @plugin  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture.register>
InstructionInfo().add_branch(BranchType.TrueBranch, TARGET)  # report a branch target from get_instruction_info  @plugin @cfg  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.InstructionInfo.add_branch>
InstructionTextToken(InstructionTextTokenType.RegisterToken, "eax")  # make one disassembly token  @plugin @render  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.InstructionTextToken>
RegisterInfo("rax", 8)                    # describe a register for a custom arch  @plugin  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.RegisterInfo>
BinaryViewType["ELF"].register_arch(ID, Endianness.LittleEndian, arch)  # map an ELF machine id to an arch  @plugin @loader  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.BinaryViewType.register_arch>
